## External dependencies

Nothing here has an install step. The plugin is QML plus three scripts, and it
depends on what Omarchy already provides:

- **Omarchy Quattro** (Quickshell/QML host) — supplies the bar, the overlay
  surface, and the plugin loader that reads `manifest.json`
- **Python 3, standard library only** — `bin/omarchy-controller-launcherd`
  imports nothing outside the stdlib, so there is no pip requirement
- **Linux evdev** (`/dev/input/event*`) — the daemon reads gamepad events
  through the kernel interface and, only while armed, holds `EVIOCGRAB`
- **bash**, **jq**, **coreutils** — used by the two helper scripts
- **Omarchy helper commands** — entries in `launchers.json` call
  `omarchy-pkg-present`, `omarchy-launch-floating-terminal-with-presentation`,
  and the `omarchy-install-gaming-*` scripts

The game launchers the wheel points at (Steam, Heroic, Lutris, RetroArch,
Prism, Moonlight, and the rest) are **not** dependencies. None is bundled or
installed by this plugin; an entry whose `installed` guard fails simply sits
inert on the wheel.

## Third-party art

The MIT grant above covers this plugin's own code and documentation. It does
**not** extend to the launcher logos in `media/`. Those are the marks of their
respective projects, reproduced only to identify the application each wheel
entry launches, and all rights in them remain with their owners.

| File(s) | Source | Upstream license |
|---|---|---|
| `steam.png`, `minecraft.png`, `geforce-now.png`, `xbox-cloud.png` | [homarr-labs/dashboard-icons](https://github.com/homarr-labs/dashboard-icons) | Apache-2.0 |
| `battlenet.png`, `retroarch.png` | [simple-icons](https://simpleicons.org) | CC0-1.0 |
| `heroic.png` | [Heroic Games Launcher](https://github.com/Heroic-Games-Launcher/HeroicGamesLauncher) | GPL-3.0 |
| `lutris.png` | [Lutris](https://github.com/lutris/lutris) | GPL-3.0 |
| `prismlauncher.png` | [Prism Launcher](https://github.com/PrismLauncher/PrismLauncher) | GPL-3.0 |
| `moonlight-dark.png`, `moonlight-light.png` | rasterised from the SVG in Arch's `moonlight-qt` package ([moonlight-qt](https://github.com/moonlight-stream/moonlight-qt)) | GPL-3.0 |

`battlenet.png`, `retroarch.png`, `moonlight-dark.png` and `moonlight-light.png`
have been recoloured to their entry's accent; the rest are unmodified.

Upstream license identifiers name the license of the source repository. Several
of these projects hold trademark rights in their names and logos independently
of that license. If you are a rights holder and object to a mark appearing
here, open an issue and it will be removed.

`screenshot.png` and `preview.png` are original work by the author and fall
under the MIT grant above.
